{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tokophobic-segregated-stinkbug","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nLive completion-gate captures show agentic runs wasting 40-70% of their request budget on DUPLICATE tool calls: one run repeated an identical search_files call 144x, another looped 62x on an honest \"(no matches)\" result. The shipped windowed distinct-ratio actuator (agent_call.py) correctly ABORTS pathological runs, but abortion is the backstop — nothing today prevents the waste before the trip point, and every duplicate re-executes the tool and re-pays the round-trip. Research across agent harnesses (OpenHands StuckDetector, smolagents max_steps) found detect-and-terminate everywhere but no harness that memoizes the duplicate and steers the model back on course — graduated nudge-then-abort is the recommended pattern.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a memoize+nudge toolset wrapper at the shared agent-call seam (src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py), the module that already arms every tool-bearing Agent call: wrapper order runaway guard OUTERMOST -> memo -> steering (guard :68, steering :45; the guard's call_tool observes the signature before the memo short-circuits, so the actuator's window math is unchanged).\n\n- Key: the EXISTING usage_log tool-call signature (identical normalization to the actuator — same signature means same dedup semantics).\n- Behavior: first repeat of a signature returns the cached result plus a static templated nudge line; further repeats return the cached result plus a stronger static nudge; the distinct-ratio actuator remains the abort backstop. Static text only — a templated nudge keeps message content byte-stable for provider prompt caching.\n- Error results are NEVER memoized: a failed call passes through on retry (legitimate retries must re-execute).\n- Read-only allowlist: only read_file, search_files, list_directory, and show_ticket are memoized (all four exist in the verifier toolset, pai_tools.py:243); write or non-deterministic tools — including the banked-verification sibling's record_criterion_verdict — are exempt.\n- In-context nudge for pre-loaded files: when the pre-loading sibling's manifest marks a file FULL, the nudge for a read_file on it says the content is already in context above; a file the manifest marks skeleton executes normally and returns the real content — the model is never denied elided bodies. Manifest absent (this ticket ships before the pre-loading sibling): no in-context nudge for any file; memoization and the generic repeat nudge still apply — no dependency on the pre-loading work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py — the memo wrapper + wrapper-order wiring (guard -> memo -> steering).\n- tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py — new: memo semantics, wrapper order, allowlist, error passthrough, nudge escalation, manifest gating.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A duplicate allowlisted call returns the cached result without re-executing the tool; the wrapped tool function runs exactly once for N identical calls (unit test with a counting stub).\n- [ ] Nudge escalation: first repeat carries the level-1 static nudge, subsequent repeats the level-2 text; both byte-stable across runs (unit test).\n- [ ] The runaway guard still observes memoized duplicates: the distinct-ratio window sees every duplicate signature, and a synthetic loop still trips the actuator at the same call index with the memo active (unit test against the existing guard tests' fixtures).\n- [ ] Error results are not memoized: a call that raised re-executes on the next identical call (unit test).\n- [ ] Only allowlisted read-only tools are memoized; record_criterion_verdict and any non-allowlisted tool always execute (unit test).\n- [ ] Manifest gating: with a manifest marking a file FULL the nudge says already-in-context; skeleton or absent manifest yields normal execution with the generic repeat nudge only (unit test).\n- [ ] Live Bedrock capture recorded on this ticket: a run demonstrating either a nudge-broken loop (duplicate signature followed by a different next call) or a nudge->actuator escalation, with usage-log figures.\n- [ ] make lint and make typecheck pass; the existing runaway-guard unit suite (tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py) passes unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit suite in tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py per the acceptance criteria (counting stubs, wrapper-order assertion, guard-interaction fixture reuse). Run: python -m pytest tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py -q. Live Bedrock capture per the live AC recorded as a ticket comment. make lint + make typecheck.","id":"f6fc-27fe-d3af-4f87","parent_id":"10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Memoize and nudge duplicate read-only tool calls at the shared agent-call seam"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786047351244680001,"uuid":"c02f3a67-eeca-4048-843d-c24429bd8ac7"}